# Flutter Generated Assets

Before adding or referencing an asset, inspect the project (`pubspec.yaml`, generated files, `dev_dependencies`) to identify the existing asset generation package (e.g. `flutter_gen`).

## Use generated classes only

Never use raw string paths. Use the generated API:

```dart
// ❌ BAD
Image.asset('assets/images/logo.png')
SvgPicture.asset('assets/images/fitflow_logo.svg')

// ✅ GOOD
Image.asset(Assets.images.logo.path)
SvgPicture.asset(Assets.images.fitflowLogo.path)
```

## If no generator is found

Stop. Do not add a generator or use raw paths. Ask which generator they prefer.

Once they answer, append the package name under **Preferred generator** in this file, then use that package.

## Preferred generator

flutter_gen_runner
